  "body": "Replacement for #773 (jenhaert's fork refused a push from this account). It carries PR 773's commits by jenhaert unchanged (head 6b9648764) plus one merge of `origin/main`. Original description: #773 (#771, stacked on #770).\n\n## What changed\nTwo orientation dropdowns, one section (`setup_orient_pick::section`): Plane orientation (Axes default, Points, Face, Manual, Cylinder angle) and Orientation point (model box, stock box, vertex). Main moved the alignment pickers off the Setups overview, so the section is mounted on each setup's own Settings page only, inside the \"Part orientation\" group. Every apply still queues its undoable command (`AlignPartCylinder`, `PlaceSetupOrigin`, the existing align commands).\n\n## Hand-resolved hunks (merge of main)\n- `crates/app/src/pick.rs`: union of the cylinder re-export and main's `lay_on_plane_in` / `lay_on_points_in`.\n- `crates/ui/src/egui_app/setup_pages.rs`: main's version (the settings body moved to `setup_settings_page.rs`, the tool table to `tool_list_page.rs`).\n- `crates/ui/src/state.rs` + `state_align.rs`: main moved the align arms into `dispatch_align` (#738). `AlignPartCylinder` is routed there (new `Draft::Cylinder`, same behaviour as before); `PlaceSetupOrigin` stays in `state.rs`.\n- `crates/ui/src/egui_app/setup_settings_page.rs`: \"Part orientation\" group now draws `setup_orient_pick::section` plus main's relative row, replacing the separate align/plane/points/axes rows (the section draws those rows itself behind its dropdown).\n- Tests follow the dropdown (assertions only, no PNG): `tests/setup_settings_page.rs` (checks Axes default, then Face, Points, Manual rows; Apply counts), `tests/plane_face_pick.rs` (switches the method before arming).\n\n## Gate that ran (worktree, CARGO_BUILD_JOBS=4)\n- `cargo test -p camcraft-ui --lib` (CWD crates/ui): 741 passed, 0 failed, 5 ignored.\n- `camcraft-app` tests `orient_dropdowns` 9, `align_compose` 3, `align_axes` 9: ok.\n- clippy `-D warnings`: camcraft-ui `--all-targets`; camcraft-app `--lib --test orient_dropdowns`: clean.\n\n## Not exercised\n`cargo xtask gate quick` itself, the ui integration test binaries outside the lib, the pixel snapshots (release lane), the GUI. The cylinder pick (`align_from_cylinder`) still reads the absolute part frame, not the #738 compose-from-held-alignment form; not changed here. No before/after screenshots (maintainer asks for them on UI PRs).\n\nChangelog: feat(ui): two orientation dropdowns on the Setups pages - plane method (axes/points/face/manual/cylinder angle) and origin point (model box/stock box/vertex), one section everywhere (#771, PR)\n\nFixes #771\n\nMCP follow-up: the tools for `AlignPartCylinder` and `PlaceSetupOrigin` are owed in issue 1586 (\"MCP: AlignPartCylinder and PlaceSetupOrigin\"), per \"Commands ship with an MCP tool\".\n\n🤖 Generated with [Claude Code](https://claude.com/claude-code)\n",
